    {
      "id": "arxiv:2611.03223",
      "date": "2026-11-02",
      "title": "Do Agents Still Follow the Rules? Benchmarking Rule Compliance under Agent Context Compaction",
      "topic": "agent",
      "language": [
        "zh",
        "en"
      ],
      "authors": [
        "Yiwei Zha",
        "Qingyu Meng",
        "Herbert Bos",
        "Min Chen"
      ],
      "institution": "Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam",
      "summary": {
        "zh": "本文引入了 ARCBench，填补了在完整智能体框架下评估规则合规性的空白。研究揭示了一个关键发现：上下文压缩导致的违规主要不是因为规则被物理删除，而是因为智能体在压缩上下文中对规则的语义理解失效或优先级判断错误。即使规则被保留，智能体也更容易违反规则。这表明未来的改进方向不应仅关注规则的信息检索保留，更应关注智能体在压缩上下文中的推理一致性和规则遵循能力。",
        "en": "- **Background**: LLM agents compact long interaction histories to fit context windows and reduce costs. However, the compacted context must retain operating rules (e.g., safety policies) that govern subsequent actions."
      },
      "links": {
        "abs": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03223v1",
        "pdf": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.03223v1",
        "github": "https://github.com/VUAISec/ARCBench"
      },
